From 1132d094d77a24df1df159c2efdf0cff759a6029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:48:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] ad5x: Keep the environment in the ota partition

The environment was at 0x8A400 and 0x92400, inside the first MiB, next
to the boot loader and the GPT, where the stock U-Boot would keep its
own. Writing it from Linux (fw_setenv) then means writing the first MiB
on every start, and a bad write there can stop the printer from
starting at all.

Keep both copies in "ota" (p5, LBA 0x6C800 in the stock SPL's table) at
512 KiB and 544 KiB into the partition (eMMC 0xD980000 and 0xD988000),
32 KiB each: clear of the boot flag (bytes 0-11, with the stock
scripts' 256-byte read) and of Kiln's boot trace (64-72 KiB). Linux
reaches them as /dev/mmcblk0p5 at 0x80000 and 0x88000.
---
 configs/ad5x_defconfig | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/ad5x_defconfig b/configs/ad5x_defconfig
index 8a55cced..5164cc1a 100644
--- a/configs/ad5x_defconfig
+++ b/configs/ad5x_defconfig
@@ -20,9 +20,9 @@ CONFIG_CMD_TIME=y
 CONFIG_VERSION_VARIABLE=y
 CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
 CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x8000
-CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x8A400
+CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0xD980000
 CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT=y
-CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND=0x92400
+CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND=0xD988000
 CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=0
 CONFIG_ENV_MMC_EMMC_HW_PARTITION=0
 CONFIG_ENV_SOURCE_FILE="ad5x"
-- 
2.56.0

